  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "MqttClient_PacketReset",
    "file": "wolfmqtt/src/mqtt_client.c",
    "description": "In WOLFMQTT_MULTITHREAD builds, MqttClient_PacketReset unconditionally adds sizeof(MqttPendResp) to the reset offset for every packet type. Response objects such as MqttConnectAck do not contain a MqttPendResp after MqttMsgStat, so their fields are not cleared (and for small objects the reset may be skipped entirely). The subsequent MQTT v5 CONNACK decode only assigns connect_ack->props when the encoded property length is nonzero. With a zero property length, the stale union bytes remain in props; Handle_Props then passes that bogus pointer to MqttProps_Free, which writes through it and crashes.",
    "conditions": "Using MqttClient_WaitMessage/WaitMessage_ex in a WOLFMQTT_V5 + WOLFMQTT_MULTITHREAD build, attacker-controlled network input must cause the shared client->msg union to contain nonzero stale bytes at the MqttConnectAck.props position and then deliver a valid MQTT v5 CONNACK whose property-length VBI is zero. MqttClient_WaitType identifies the CONNACK, calls the faulty reset on client->msg, and decodes it into that shared object; because no properties are decoded, props retains the stale value (0x202020202020 in this PoV), which Handle_Props attempts to free."
  },
